# Figure 31, DRAW views of ImageDemo.in: the telescope and relay lens, elements 0-8, and the relay close-up 6-8 in
# the XZ plane.  The plane-parallel plate (9-10, Kr 1e22, no aperture) and the Return surfaces (11-12) draw as
# kilometre-sized V shapes and swamp the view (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (bb); Dave 2026-10-19: 'figure 31 is a mess'), on the /png
# device (giza writes a page when the next one opens, so the last view is drawn twice).  Pages land in
# build/figs/fig31/; tools/regen_engine_figs.py puts the two views side by side as media/fig_rescued_31.png.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/ImageDemo.in fig31
cd $TMP/fig31
old ImageDemo.in
pgd
/png
draw
0
8
xz
draw
6
8
xz
draw
6
8
xz
! mkdir -p $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/build/figs/fig31; cp $TMP/fig31/giza_*.png $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/build/figs/fig31/
